cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GenClass Runtime in your work, please cite it with these metadata and name the version of @genclass/runtime you used."
type: software
title: "GenClass Runtime"
abstract: >-
  GenClass Runtime (@genclass/runtime) is an open-source (Apache-2.0) browser library that reports race
  conditions in web apps while they happen: stale responses that land over newer data, duplicate requests such as
  double submits, inconsistent state and failure storms. A small model runs on the user's device, in a Web Worker on
  WebGPU or WASM, and each report comes with its evidence. By default it only reports (observe): it never holds,
  delays or changes a request, a response or a state write. The opt-in guard mode may act on a few of them, and
  heal is experimental.
authors:
  - name: "Daybot Solutions Inc."
    website: "https://genclass.dev"
repository-code: "https://github.com/genclass-dev/GenClass-lib"
url: "https://genclass.dev"
license: Apache-2.0
# The newest published release of @genclass/runtime (npm `beta`; `latest` is 0.2.2, dated 2026-10-13 in the
# CHANGELOG and published to npm on 2026-10-15, before this one).
# Update both fields at each release.
version: "0.3.0-beta.0"
date-released: "2026-10-15"
keywords:
  - race condition
  - stale response
  - double submit
  - web app
  - browser
  - runtime monitoring
  - on-device model
  - WebGPU
  - WebAssembly
